  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4be51c5168caa0d42bd51f33c68daba8, type: 3}
  m_Name: Gate Keeper's Last Word
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::LetterData
  letterTitle: 
  pages:
  - "I swear on the old gods I heard them again last night. Not wolves. These things
    sounded twisted\u2026 like men trying to howl through broken throats. Maybe it\u2019s
    the drink getting into my head. Maybe the woods truly got something living in
    them now. Be that as it may, come down to the tavern one evening and see it yourself.
    Finest drink this side of the river, I mean it. Those refugee folk may be strange,
    but by the gods they know how to brew proper liquor. And Fox--The woman\u2019s
    carved by drunken sails. Nearly dropped my cup when she leaned over the counter.
    Truth be told they could hold more drinks than mine. Hah!\r\nStrange thing is,
    I woke the next morning with my head split and couldn\u2019t find the cult gate
    keys anywhere. Don\u2019t remember half the things I said either. Foxy kept laughing
    saying I was rambling all night like some washed-up sailor .If you see me before
    patrol, help me look around the docks a bit. Priest'll skin me alive if those
    keys stay missing."
  letterImage: {fileID: 0}
